[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4702713074","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114798#issuecomment-4702713074","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114798","id":4702713074,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABGE208g","user":{"login":"ThomasProg","id":39605375,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NjA1Mzc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39605375?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasProg","html_url":"https://github.com/ThomasProg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasProg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasProg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasProg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasProg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasProg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasProg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasProg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasProg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasProg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-14T18:52:42Z","updated_at":"2026-06-14T18:52:42Z","body":"Thanks for the fix @Ivorforce !\r\nI'm using LocalVector a lot and it's really painful not being able to call `back()` or `pop_back()`, I hope this will be merged soon.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4702713074/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5010718046","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114798#issuecomment-5010718046","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114798","id":5010718046,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKql9Xg","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-18T09:15:01Z","updated_at":"2026-07-18T09:15:01Z","body":"Went on a little rabbit hole to why STL vector doesn't return on `pop_back`:\r\n\r\n* If the copy / move of T throws an exception on returning from `pop_back`, the value would be lost forever, and that violates their principle not to modify on failure\r\n* `back()` can return a reference, and it can't fail (as long as not empty). I suppose reference could be faster than by value for large types (although you'd have to destroy the T anyway, so whether this makes any overall difference I don't know)\r\n\r\nSo I don't *think* `pop_back` returning T should be a problem for us as a convenience function, and less verbose.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5010718046/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]